LABMIDDLEWARE
Enterprise Technical Documentation

Version: 1.0
Author: Josue Sierra
Repository: https://github.com/JosueSR2

OVERVIEW

LabMiddleware is an enterprise-grade laboratory integration middleware designed to interface clinical analyzers with Laboratory Information Systems (LIS) such as OpenELIS.

The system provides protocol-level handling, message transformation, transport abstraction, and secure delivery mechanisms to ensure reliable laboratory data exchange.

This middleware is intended for:

Clinical laboratories

Hospital environments

Diagnostic centers

LIS integration projects

Analyzer simulation and validation environments

SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

Logical Architecture:

Analyzer Layer
↓
Transport Layer (TCP / Serial / File)
↓
Protocol Engine (HL7 MLLP / ASTM)
↓
Parsing & Transformation Engine
↓
Delivery Engine (REST API)
↓
Laboratory Information System (LIS)

Core Components:

Transport Listener

TCP Listener

Serial Port Listener

File System Watcher

Protocol Processor

HL7 MLLP framing handler

ASTM frame handler (STX/ETX + checksum)

Message Parser

Segment extraction

Result mapping

Validation layer

Delivery Engine

REST client

Retry policy

Batch delivery

Circuit breaker support

Logging & Monitoring

Configurable verbosity

Error tracking

Delivery auditing

SUPPORTED COMMUNICATION METHODS

3.1 TCP/IP

Used for:

HL7 MLLP analyzers

ASTM over TCP analyzers

Configurable parameters:

Port

Encoding

TLS support (optional)

3.2 Serial / USB

Used for:

Legacy analyzers

Direct serial communication devices

Configurable parameters:

PortName

BaudRate

Parity

DataBits

StopBits

3.3 File Drop

Used for:

Offline analyzers

Batch export systems

Testing environments

Monitors a configured directory and processes incoming files.

SUPPORTED PROTOCOLS

4.1 HL7 (MLLP)

Message framing:

Start Block: 0x0B (VT)
End Block: 0x1C (FS) + 0x0D (CR)

Supported message structure:

MSH

PID

OBR

OBX

Features:

UTF-8 support

Automatic message boundary detection

ACK generation support (if enabled)

4.2 ASTM

Frame structure:

STX
Frame number
Data
ETX
Checksum
CR LF

Features:

Checksum validation

ACK / NAK handling

Multi-frame message reconstruction

CONFIGURATION

Primary configuration file: appsettings.json

Example:

{
"Middleware": {
"LisUrl": "https://localhost:8443/api/OpenELIS-Global/analyzer/astm
",
"DeliveryBatchSize": 50,
"RetryScheduleSeconds": [10, 30, 120, 300],
"Tcp": {
"Enabled": true,
"Port": 5001
},
"Serial": {
"Enabled": false,
"PortName": "COM1",
"BaudRate": 9600
},
"Analyzers": [
{
"Name": "hl7-mllp-default",
"Transport": "Tcp",
"Protocol": "Hl7Mllp",
"TcpPort": 5001,
"EncodingName": "utf-8"
},
{
"Name": "astm-tcp-default",
"Transport": "Tcp",
"Protocol": "Astm",
"TcpPort": 5002,
"EncodingName": "ascii"
}
]
}
}

Key Configuration Areas:

LIS endpoint configuration

Transport activation

Analyzer-to-port mapping

Encoding definition

Retry policies

Security configuration

SECURITY

Supported Security Features:

HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)

Basic Authentication

Bearer Token Authentication

Optional certificate validation override

Configurable HTTP timeouts

Circuit breaker protection

Recommended production setup:

TLS enabled

Valid server certificate

Authentication enabled

Logging level set to INFO

Circuit breaker enabled

DELIVERY AND RESILIENCE

The Delivery Engine includes:

Configurable retry schedule

Batched result submission

Circuit breaker protection

Timeout configuration

Outbox persistence (SQLite supported)

Retry Strategy Example:
10s → 30s → 120s → 300s

LOGGING AND MONITORING

Logging levels:

ERROR

WARN

INFO

DEBUG

Logs include:

Connection events

Protocol parsing results

Delivery attempts

Retry triggers

Failure diagnostics

Docker log example:

docker logs --tail 100 -f openelisglobal-middlewares

DEPLOYMENT

Supported Environments:

Docker container

Windows Service (if implemented)

Linux service deployment

On-premise server environments

Recommended Deployment Architecture:

Analyzer Network Segment
↓
Middleware Server
↓
Secure Channel (HTTPS)
↓
LIS Server

USE CASES

Hematology analyzer integration

Biochemistry analyzer integration

Multi-analyzer hospital environments

Laboratory simulation platforms

OpenELIS integration projects

Analyzer validation and testing labs

